# Digest-bound sources must hash identically across platforms.
#
# This repository's provenance rests on sha256 digests: vendored skill contracts
# carry the digest of the upstream bytes they came from, and the germination
# invitation is verified against a recorded digest rather than an assertion.
#
# Git's autocrlf conversion would rewrite line endings in the working tree,
# which changes those digests without changing a word of content. Pinning LF
# here keeps a digest a fact about content rather than about which machine
# happened to check the file out.
#
# The tooling also normalizes newlines before hashing, so an unpinned or
# hand-copied file still verifies. The redundancy is deliberate: the pin keeps
# digests stable, and the normalization keeps an honest transmission from being
# mistaken for tampering.

* text=auto eol=lf

docs/skill-drafts/** text eol=lf
lineage/invitation-received.md text eol=lf
vendor-manifest.json text eol=lf
tools/*.py text eol=lf
